# Claude Code OAuth token — get one by running `claude setup-token` on your host.
# Lets the agent use your Claude subscription instead of an API key.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# Or use an Anthropic API key instead — uncomment and fill in:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GitHub personal access token — sandboxes authenticate with it to read and
# manage GitHub Issues and open PRs. Sandcastle forwards this file into each
# sandbox, so the token reaches the agent there. Host-side `gh`/`git` calls use
# your ambient credential (`gh auth`), not this value.
# Create a fine-grained token: https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
# Required repository permissions: Contents (Read and write), Issues (Read and
# write), Pull requests (Read and write), and Metadata (Read).
GH_TOKEN=
